01:26:12,000 --> 01:26:14,025
...wasn't me.

959
01:26:16,704 --> 01:26:18,365
It doesn't matter what Lucy said.

960
01:26:18,540 --> 01:26:22,340
I stopped trusting her after she stole
my Pop Rocks in the third grade.

961
01:26:24,212 --> 01:26:25,907
Matt.

962
01:26:27,882 --> 01:26:33,286
I am not the awful person
that I know that I was.

963
01:26:33,454 --> 01:26:35,718
I don't even know that person.

964
01:26:37,225 --> 01:26:39,853
And I'd like to believe....

965
01:26:40,028 --> 01:26:43,725
I have to believe
that if you knew that...

966
01:26:43,898 --> 01:26:47,959
...if in your heart, you really,
really knew that...

967
01:26:49,103 --> 01:26:51,833
...you wouldn't be getting ready
to marry someone now.

968
01:26:52,006 --> 01:26:55,703
Unless that someone were me.

969
01:27:08,189 --> 01:27:12,023
Jenna, I'm not gonna lie to you.

970
01:27:14,562 --> 01:27:17,053
I have felt things...

971
01:27:17,232 --> 01:27:19,530
...these past few weeks...

972
01:27:20,668 --> 01:27:23,967
...that I didn't know I could
feel anymore.

973
01:27:24,939 --> 01:27:28,898
But I have realized
in these past few days...

974
01:27:30,945 --> 01:27:34,176
...you can't just turn back time.

975
01:27:35,750 --> 01:27:38,116
Why not?

976
01:27:38,286 --> 01:27:39,913
I moved on.

977
01:27:40,088 --> 01:27:41,487
You moved on.

978
01:27:41,823 --> 01:27:45,088
We've gone down different paths
for so long.

979
01:27:45,260 --> 01:27:47,956
We made choices.

980
01:27:48,129 --> 01:27:50,962
I chose Wendy.

981
01:27:52,800 --> 01:27:55,598
That's her family down there.

982
01:27:56,204 --> 01:27:58,832
We care about each other,
you know?

983
01:28:00,708 --> 01:28:05,202
You don't always get the dream
house, but you get awfully close.

984
01:28:09,150 --> 01:28:11,482
Please don't cry, Jenna.

985
01:28:11,653 --> 01:28:14,554
Oh, I'll be fine, I promise.

986
01:28:44,919 --> 01:28:46,944
Matty, can I have it?

987
01:28:47,121 --> 01:28:48,782
Please?

988
01:28:48,956 --> 01:28:51,254
-You're not gonna whip it at me?
-No.

989
01:28:58,933 --> 01:29:02,232
Look, I won't have you be late.
Just go.

990
01:29:02,704 --> 01:29:06,162
Go on. I'm fine. I'm just crying
because I'm happy.

991
01:29:06,341 --> 01:29:09,401
I want you to be so, so happy.

992
01:29:11,946 --> 01:29:14,073
I love you, Matt.

993
01:29:17,418 --> 01:29:19,215
You're my best friend.

994
01:29:21,856 --> 01:29:24,017
Jenna, l....

995
01:29:25,193 --> 01:29:27,718
I've always loved you.

996
01:31:30,151 --> 01:31:33,086
Jenna's waiting for you in the closet.

997
01:31:44,131 --> 01:31:45,996
Matty.

998
01:31:52,940 --> 01:31:55,204
You really know what you're doing.

999
01:31:55,776 --> 01:31:58,006
Come on.

1000
01:31:59,146 --> 01:32:01,876
-Sorry, I forgot my scarf.
-You know what?

1001
01:32:02,049 --> 01:32:06,213
You can be the pot and kettle
all by yourself from now on, biatch.

1002
01:32:06,387 --> 01:32:07,820
Come on, Matt.

1003
01:32:07,989 --> 01:32:10,219
-What did you call me?
-We're gonna be late.

1004
01:32:10,391 --> 01:32:12,256
-For what?
-You'll see.

1005
01:33:05,780 --> 01:33:07,680
A Razzle, Mr. Flamhaff?

1006
01:33:07,848 --> 01:33:10,214
Thank you, Mrs. Flamhaff.


